            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jldub"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A very good recipe as is. Not as thick as I am used to though. To make it a 5-star recipe, I added finely chopped cucumbers, and I left out the olive oil and used greek yogurt because it is thicker. If you can't find greek yogurt (or a real yogurt strainer), you can put two coffee filters into a colander. Put the colander over a bowl and strain the yogurt for about an hour or so on the countertop."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "keiram"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tripled the recipe and used Greek yogurt. Then to make a thicker dip I added 8oz regular cream cheese, 8oz Greek yogurt cream cheese, more salt, pepper, olive oil, and lemon. I used a food processor to cream the mixture. Lastly I used the pulse setting to mix in finely diced (seeded) cucumber. Great dip!",
            "datePublished": "2014-10-31T02:40:40.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "D GISB"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is a great base but requires additional steps and ingredients to make it perfect. I bought 16 oz of yogurt, lined a sieve with paper towel and placed the yogurt in it. After a few hours all of the liquid drained out of the yogurt leaving it nice and thick. I added 1 cup of grated Long English Cucumber. Be sure to squeeze all of the liquid out of the cucmber after grating it. I also added 1 tablespoon of chopped fresh mint.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-23T14:55:25.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pamela"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easy to make and delicious! I added a deseeded, peeled, and grated cucumber as others recommended. I also used plain greek yogurt instead of straining regular yogurt. Definitely gets better as it sits so leave it in the fridge overnight if possible. I used these on baked falafel burgers but am already planning to make spicy lamb burgers to use the rest of the sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2015-03-10T10:54:44.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "To make this a true tzatziki sauce, I did add one very large deseeded cucumber. I also used greek yogurt. VERY good. I seriously ate myself sick on this with a bag of sea salt pita chips. NOTE: If you can stand it, the longer this sauce sits.......the better it gets.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-12T02:47:23.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Melanie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I can eat this 24/7. I used Greek yogurt and added chopped cucumber and since I have mint in my yard, added that too. I dip in pita bread. Soooooo good!",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-02T20:02:12.670Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rebecca"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added 3/4 cucumber with water squeezed out and a half teaspoon of Turkish red chili flakes",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-31T12:44:18.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "heatherjeanmcc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is great, i make it all the time to accompany bbq chicken, kabobs, or sweet potato fries. As other reviewers have suggested, i finely shred 1/2 a cucumber and add. Of course, try to dry the shredded cucumber as best as possible, otherwise the tzatziki is too watery. Using a balkan-style yogurt also makes it more authentic.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-30T17:54:43.330Z"
          },
          {
